    "output_tokens": 447
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 8,
   "response_text": "The training configuration doesn't include any learning rate schedule. Given that:\n\n1. The final epoch shows a dramatic drop in validation accuracy (0.8465 \u2192 0.7998)\n2. The training loss at epoch 19 also increases (0.3598 \u2192 0.3846)\n3. There is no learning rate decay or scheduling configured\n4. A learning rate of 0.1 for Adam is on the high side and can cause instability over many epochs\n\nThis indicates a **missing or insufficient learning rate schedule**. The model is likely experiencing divergence or severe overfitting in the final epoch due to the constant high learning rate.\n\nLet me verify there's no learning rate schedule implementation in the code:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_017oiWFwrgVHLufAPVubunRm",
